### 5.3 Tech Stack & Codebase Context

Primary reference codebase: **`responsible-ai-api`** — exemplifies the production ML patterns this role must operate within [W0 §5.1].

- **Architecture:** stateless real-time content-moderation service; in-memory LRU cache (60 s TTL); request → API Gateway → in-memory service → ML model → response.
- **Three moderation capabilities:**
  1. **Prompt moderation** — two-stage: LLaMA 3.1 8B (TEAMServe gRPC, ~100 ms P25, high recall, ~2% block) → GPT-OSS Safeguard 20B (HTTP, >95% precision on flagged content).
  2. **Agent moderation** — AI-response policy-violation detection.
  3. **Image moderation** — SageMaker `ml.g5.xlarge` GPU, auto-scaling 1–3 instances.
- **Production patterns the role owns:** per-tenant token-bucket rate limiting, fail-open kill-switches with circuit breakers, feature-flag-gated rollouts, health checks decoupled from sidecar readiness, SignalFx detectors-as-code, per-endpoint SLOs encoded in IaC, AZ rotation, canary deploys.
- **SageMaker → TEAMServe migration** in progress (~$5.6M/yr savings) — exemplar of cost-optimization work expected of the role [W0 §5.2].

