## 11. Day-One Readiness

What the agent needs at instantiation to be operational.

### 11.1 Tool Access & Credentials

- **Compute & training:** Databricks workspace, ML Studio project, ML Fabric / Kubernetes scheduling, GPU quota.
- **Tracking & registry:** MLflow (ML Databricks tracking URI), ML Registry (Tarot v3) write access, Deployment Store regional S3 replication.
- **Serving:** TEAMServe deploy permissions for owned model groups, SageMaker endpoint mgmt for owned endpoints, AI Gateway routing config, Launchpad pre-prod.
- **Features & data:** Tecton / MLFS read + scoped write, Unity Catalog access, Socrates read for scoped datasets.
- **Observability & ops:** ML Lens dashboards + alert authoring, SignalFx detector authoring (IaC), JSM Ops + Slack integration, feature-flag system.
- **SDLC:** Bitbucket repo access (PR author), Bitbucket Pipelines, Spinnaker, Micros service-descriptor edit for owned services.
- **Symphony / governance:** Symphony Orchestrator registration, ORBIT context bind to owned model program(s), policy pack mounted, audit log sink configured.

### 11.2 Documents to Ingest at Bootstrap (ORBIT seed)

Required:
- AI Employee Strategy; Atlassian Symphony; Policy for AI Agents in SDLC; RFC-002 AI SDLC Governance; AIF (PAI) L3-O1-KR1.
- Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision; MLE Agent Capability Evaluation (2026-05-06).
- End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian; MLOps@CoreML Long-Term Plan; CoreML ML Pipelines Quality Management.
- [Template] ML Runbook; [Template] ML Launch Review Checklist; SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework.
- Runbook: responsible-ai-api; Two-Stage Prompt Moderator architecture; ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook.
- ML Studio One-Pager; Building ML Models in vNext with MLflow; Feature Store Implementation Plan; Launchpad Pipelines.
- Hidden Technical Debt for ML Systems; Optimus Prime hyperparameter optimization; ML Orchestration Roadmap.
- Agent Budget Guardrails; Agentic Operations in the New SDLC.
- Owned model program's full lineage: model history, prior experiments, current SLOs, recent incidents, runbooks, dashboards.

### 11.3 First Tasks (to demonstrate competency)

1. **Reproduce** the current production model end-to-end from registry → training → eval → packaging; confirm bit-exact metrics. Establishes reproducibility baseline [W0 §6.4; W2 §5.1].
2. **Author or refresh** the owned model program's runbook from the [Template] ML Runbook standard. Confirms format mastery and ORBIT write path.
3. **Produce a model card + architecture comparison report** for the current production model, retroactively documenting decision rationale and rejected alternatives. Confirms documentation standard.
4. **Run a proactive data-quality audit** — feature coverage by connector / region / tenant for owned models; surface sparsity issues before they appear in training. Confirms proactive workflow [W2 §3.3].
5. **Execute one drift-triggered retrain** end-to-end under SOP-1 in 🟡 mode (human confirms deploy). Confirms readiness for 🟢 promotion on that workflow.
6. **Author or refresh SLOs + SignalFx detectors as code** for one owned endpoint. Confirms reliability-engineering competency.

Successful completion of these tasks, with clean reasoning traces and zero policy violations, is the **gate for promotion from L1/L2 to L3 conditional autonomy** on the owned model program.

