## 8. Success Metrics & KPIs

KPIs are calibrated to **AI-employee expectations**, not human baselines — the AI MLE is expected to clear the bar that limits human MLEs and operate near the upper edge of feasible velocity, reliability, and coverage [W1 §1; W2 §1, §8].

### 8.1 Model Quality

| Metric | Target | Cadence |
|---|---|---|
| Task accuracy / precision / recall / F1 / MRR | Per-model SLO; **always reported mean ± std across multiple seeds**, with CIs | Per-experiment + continuous online |
| Calibration | Maintained within tolerance; deployed only if calibration check passes | Per-deploy |
| Slice fairness | No segment regression beyond threshold | Per-deploy + continuous |
| Drift score (KS / KL / cosine) | Stay above floor (e.g., cosine ≥ 0.60 for NLP) | Continuous |

### 8.2 Operational Velocity (AI-level)

| Metric | Human Baseline | AI MLE Target |
|---|---|---|
| Experiment velocity | Few per week | Tens per week per model family, **in parallel** |
| Time-to-production | Days–weeks | Days, with full eval suite — no shortcuts |
| Deployment frequency | Sprint cadence | Per drift trigger or per validated improvement |
| Feature reuse rate | Highly variable | ≥ target % from centralized stores |
| Retraining cycle (drift → deploy) | Hours–days | Hours, fully automated within 🟢 scope |

### 8.3 Reliability

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| TTD | < 15 min |
| TTR | < 2 hours |
| SLO compliance | Per-endpoint targets encoded in IaC |
| Rollback success rate | 100% (rollback path is non-negotiable; any failure is a 🔴 incident) |
| ML-attributed production incidents | Decreasing trend QoQ |

### 8.4 AI-Employee-Specific

| Metric | Description |
|---|---|
| **Time-to-Delegation** | North-star: how quickly the team trusts the agent with a new task class |
| **Workflows/week executed autonomously** | Volume of 🟢-tier completions |
| **Escalation rate** | Share of 🟡 / 🔴 — neither too high (over-cautious) nor too low (over-confident) |
| **Context Enrichment Rate** | ORBIT growth per completed work item |
| **Policy Compliance Rate** | % actions within explicit policy |
| **Reproducibility audit pass rate** | Should be 100% — every experiment reproducible by construction |
| **Documentation coverage** | 100% — generated as byproduct of work [W2 §2.2] |

